#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:2
msgid "i2c interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `i2c` interface permits access to a specific I2C controller. It's "
"intended to be used with Ubuntu Core and its scope and specification are "
"defined as part of the {ref}`gadget snap <reference-development-yaml-schemas-"
"the-gadget-snap>` for the deployed Ubuntu Core image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"Hardware IO interfaces covers some general considerations common to these "
"kinds of devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"To permit access, the application snaps define an i2c *plug* which is "
"associated with a corresponding and identically-named i2c *slot* in the "
"gadget snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"Using the `i2c` interface does not require Store approval and permission, "
"but usage **is** restricted because it provides privileged access to "
"hardware devices. Enabling the `i2c` interface to auto-connect can be "
"managed in the [dashboard](https://dashboard.snapcraft.io). The snap user "
"can also access a specific i2c device with a {ref}`manual interface "
"connection <explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:15
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:17
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:17
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:20
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:22
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:19
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:20
msgid ""
"**`path` (plug, slot)**: path to i2c device node.</br> Example: `path: /dev/"
"i2c-0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"**`sysfs-name` (plug, slot)**: a proper name found in `/sys/bus/i2c/"
"devices`</br> Example: `sysfs-name: 1-0050`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"Only one of `path` or `sysfs-name` should be used in either the plug or slot "
"definition, but both must match. That is to say, if the gadget declares the "
"slot-side using `sysfs-name`, the snap declaring the plug-side must also use "
"`sysfs-name`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:27
msgid ""
"The slot-side of the interface is used to derive which i2c node in `/dev/` "
"is provided to the plug-side of the connection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:29
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  i2c-1:\n"
"    interface: i2c\n"
"    path: /dev/i2c-1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:36
msgid ""
"To prevent connection to arbitrary i2c slots, the plug and slot must share "
"the same i2c attribute, including the name of the plug and slot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:38
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  i2c-1:\n"
"    interface: i2c\n"
"    path: /dev/i2c-1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:45
msgid ""
"When the slot and plug are connected, a udev rule is automatically generated "
"and tagged for the plug side for the device path, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:47
msgid "KERNEL==\"i2c-1\", TAG+=\"snap_client-snap_app-accessing-1-port\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/i2c-interface.md:51
msgid ""
"The test code for the interface is in the snapd repository: [https://"
"github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/i2c_test.go]"
"(https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/"
"i2c_test.go) The source code for the interface is in the snapd repository: "
"[https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/i2c.go]"
"(https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/i2c.go)"
msgstr ""
